url: "https://github.com/muditbhargava66/Advanced-Image-Sensor-Interface"
abstract: >
  The Advanced Image Sensor Interface is a Python simulation and interface
  framework for modeling and validating multi-protocol camera systems. It
  provides packet-level simulations of MIPI CSI-2, CoaXPress, GigE Vision, and
  USB3 Vision, together with an explicit frame codec and capture-to-processing
  pipeline that stores unpacked 8- to 20-bit samples and reports measured
  latency and throughput. The image-processing layer returns typed signal, HDR,
  RAW, lens-correction, and stereo-depth results, and adds native numpy/scipy
  camera calibration, multi-sensor synchronization, and power-management
  modeling. Version 4.0.0 introduces real AES-GCM authenticated encryption
  through an optional security extra, fail-closed integrity verification, and
  stricter processing-format validation. The framework targets algorithm
  development, protocol validation, benchmarking, and education; it simulates
  hardware behavior and is not a production camera driver or hardware PHY
  implementation.
keywords:
  - image sensor
  - image processing
  - MIPI CSI-2
  - CoaXPress
  - GigE Vision
  - USB3 Vision
  - stereo depth
  - camera calibration
  - protocol simulation
  - AES-GCM
  - Python
